    <name>
      <text>Determining the indefinite Integral</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Determine the Indefinite Integral \(\displaystyle \int {@quest_expr@}\,dx\)</p>
<p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>Given \(\displaystyle \int {@quest_expr@}\,dx\) </p>
<p>Expanding the function and dividing through by denominator, we have</p>
<p>\( \displaystyle \int ({@cc*x^3/x@}+{@bb*x/x@}+{@aa/x@})\;dx\)</p>
<p>Applying Linearity</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle {@cc@} \int x^2dx +{@aa@} \int \frac{1}{x}\,dx+{@bb@} \int dx\)</p>
<p>Solving by Integration</p>
<p>\({@sol2@}+{@soln3@}+{@soln4@}\)</p>
<p>Thus, the solution is</p>
<p> \(\displaystyle \int {@quest_expr@}\,dx ={@ta@}\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
